b","position":"1785721827970068001-398b5bc1-9612-4ed4-a1a3-b9dfc6f64324"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"06444ffd20c32342c61981a0821a754e6aee0a4751f59b7f317a9617bd75f752","event_uuid":"5acc3fcd-b33a-4e4e-93cb-0af7c3ee9716","position":{"commit_sha":"20d5b0ccca36c74458ebe73efe092c2f7be833cb","position":"1785721828573911001-5acc3fcd-b33a-4e4e-93cb-0af7c3ee9716"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1785640049516742001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"c9ef753a-b953-4058-9d3c-6558b43a089a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8c66-2e81-d5ae-4e3e"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nInert-config class (281f, 9d7a family): a typed schema field ships with zero cfg.<section>.<field> read sites outside schema/config plumbing, so the knob silently does nothing. Env vars are already covered by the docs/env-vars.md drift gate; schema fields have no equivalent.\n\n## Approach\nDeterministic AST-level check: for each field in _config_schema.py, require >=1 attribute-read site outside the schema/config plumbing modules.\n\nDetection shape (decisive, receiver-agnostic): an ast.Attribute node in Load context whose terminal attribute name equals the field name — matching ONLY on the final `.field` segment, never on a receiver spelling. This deliberately matches every real read shape in src/: `load_config().mcp.readonly`, `config.load_config(root).verify.overlap_enabled`, a section object bound to a local (`mcp_cfg.auth_introspection_endpoint`), `self.config.<section>.<field>`, or any alias. Trade-off, stated openly: terminal-name matching is permissive — an unrelated object's same-named attribute also counts, silently keeping the gate quiet. That failure mode is fail-QUIET (a rare shadowed name suppresses a firing), never a false fire on a live field; zero-reference firing stays sound because a field with literally no `.field` attribute read anywhere cannot be read. Same-named-field collisions across sections are likewise fail-quiet and accepted. Dynamic reads (getattr dispatch) are invisible to the AST walk by design — that is exactly what the marker is for. Escape hatch: '# read-via: <path-or-reason>' comment on the field for indirect reads (getattr dispatch, client-project-only knobs) — pointer required, not a bare boolean. Fires ONLY on zero references (the bug condition), so refactors that move reads cannot FP. Failing message teaches the escape and cites in-file examples. Wire into CI alongside existing gates.\n\n## Scope\n- new check script (AST walk over src/rebar) + CI wiring\n- '# read-via:' markers for any legitimately indirect current fields (enumerate at implementation; expected small)\n\n## Testing\nUnit: field with a read passes; field with zero reads fails naming the field; read-via marker with pointer passes; marker without pointer fails. Full-tree run clean at merge.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] CI fails when any schema field has zero read sites and no read-via marker; message teaches remediation.\n- [ ] Marker requires a pointer/reason; bare markers rejected.\n- [ ] Zero-reference-only firing (no change-detector behavior on refactors).\n- [ ] Tree clean at landing with justified markers only.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review","reason":"DET check wiring"},{"path":"src/rebar/config.py","reason":"config key read-path introspection"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","2f4c-7e5c-e782-4e97"],["relates_to","8c66-2e81-d5ae-4e3e"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2f4c-7e5c-e782-4e97","parent_status_uuid":"398b5bc1-9612-4ed4-a1a3-b9dfc6f64324","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["gates","config"],"ticket_id":"6754-a380-7ce1-4bf4","ticket_type":"story","title":"Config-is-read DET check: every _config_schema.py field must have a read site","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["9b58f884-837e-48d1-be53-00351869270e","8dfada99-bc4c-4be8-9b56-6710ed87d04d","e8c7cdc5-d280-4b69-9d32-9def6c7c78e4","05f5989c-3a8a-44b6-9063-23d29501c01f","398b5bc1-9612-4ed4-a1a3-b9dfc6f64324","5acc3fcd-b33a-4e4e-93cb-0af7c3ee9716","c9ef753a-b953-4058-9d3c-6558b43a089a"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785723070134628248,"uuid":"b40f44c8-181b-4aeb-bbb0-b09df778373f"}